{
  "configuration_id": "config_003",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_009: multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, concat → 61.9% acc, 36.42 GPU hrs), evidence is extremely sparse. The most critical uncertainty is whether the multimodal fusion is actually adding value over the image modality alone. Config_003 (image_only, multiprofile, resnet50, avgpool) is a clean ablation of config_009 that removes only the RNA branch while keeping the same image encoder, profile setting, and aggregation. This directly tests whether the ~62% accuracy is driven by the image features or genuinely benefits from RNA fusion. If image_only approaches 62%, we know RNA adds little and should invest in better image encoders; if it drops substantially, multimodal fusion is confirmed as the right direction and we should explore better RNA encoders and fusion strategies. Expected cost is moderate-to-low (~20-25 GPU hrs) since it omits RNA processing entirely, making it a cheap and high-information experiment that preserves budget for later exploitation."
}

